ferent suit from main W tiles \u2014 they are isolated unless we get T4/T7. But the other player\u2019s melds show across player has J3 pung, next player no melds, previous no melds \u2014 so T4, T7 still available somewhat.  \n\nBetter to keep hand more flexible: discard F2 maybe? But F2 gives potential fan if draw. Also T5, T6 might be easier to discard to avoid All Simples? Let\u2019s check:  \n\nIf discard T5 or T6, then hand has mostly W suit + honors, could aim for Half Flush (W + honors) \u2014 need to get rid of both T5 and T6 eventually. So discard one T now.  \n\nBetween T5 and T6 \u2014 similar. Choose T6 because T6 has 4 total unseen, so safe discard.  \n\nAlso W5 W6 W7 possible chow \u2014 but W5 and W6 only 1 each. Could keep W5 W7 and hope W6 for chow, but W6 I have only 1. Better to keep W3\u00d72, W5, W6, W7 as potential W chows and pairs.  \n\nBut safest: discard T6 now, keep T5 in case T4/T7 comes.  \n\nAlternatively, discard T5.  \n\nChecking opponents\u2019 discards:  \nNext player played B4, B1, B1, F1, W1, W1, B4 \u2014 so W1 dead, F1 dead.  \nAcross player played B7, B2, W4, W9, B9, W2, W7, F4, T4, T8, T1 \u2014 so T4 dead, W7 dead? W7 just one discard, maybe safe.  \nPrev player played B2, F2, T1, J2, W1, T8, W6, T9, B3, T9, W9, F3 \u2014 so W6 discarded, W6 may be safe-ish.  \n\nGiven W6 was discarded by prev player recently, maybe keeping W6 is less useful (only 2 left unseen, harder to get). Discard W6? But then W5 and W7 become isolated singles.  \n\nActually, W5, W6, W7 is possible chow if we draw W4 or W8 \u2014 but W4 in meld already, only W8 possible for W6 W7 W8. And W8 is 4 left unseen. So not great.  \n\nBetter to think:  \nIf discard W6:  \nHand: W3\u00d72, W5, W7, T5, T6, F2. Still T5 T6 cluttering.  \n\nIf discard T6:  \nHand: W3\u00d72, W5, W6, W7, T5, F2. Still have T5 and F2 to discard later.  \n\nBest plan: go for All Types \u2014 need each suit + winds/dragons. Already have W, T, and F (F3 pung), so maybe keep F2 for Seat wind pung chance. But F2 only 1 left, so maybe unlikely.  \n\nGiven this, best discard is T6 \u2014 reduces tile types to two suits + honors, but still aim for flexibility.  \n\n---\n\n**Safety**:  \nT6 has 4 left unseen, not recently discarded by others, relatively safe.  \nW6 was discarded by prev player, so maybe not safe for others to win? But W6 might be safe for discard too.  \n\nBut discard T6 keeps more W tiles together for possible chow.  \n\n---\n\n**Final decision**: Discard T6.  \n\n---\n\nEvaluation: I need to improve hand flexibility and reduce isolated tiles; T6 is less connected and safe to discard.  \nReason: Keeping W tiles together offers better chance for chows, T6 is surplus with only one companion T5.  \nAnswer: Play T6"}
