kely.\n- Two Terminal Chows (1 point) if we have chows 123 and 789 in same suit. We don't have that.\n- Mixed Double Chow (1 point) if we have two chows in different suits with same numbers. Not likely.\n- Pung of Terminals or Honors: we already have F3 pung (1 point). If we get a F1 pung, that's another 1 point, and also Prevalent Wind (2 points) for F1 pung. So that's valuable.\n- All Simples (2 points) if no terminals and honors. But we have honors (F1, F3 pung), so not.\n- No Honors (1 point) if no honor tiles, but we have honors, so not.\n- One Voided Suit (1 point) if exactly two suits. Currently we have W and T (if we keep T6) and honors, but honors are not a suit. For One Voided Suit, it considers only the three suited suits: Characters, Bamboos, Dots. We have W (Characters) and T (Bamboos), and no B (Dots), so that qualifies if we finish with only W and T? Actually the pattern is \"A hand with exactly two of the three suits of tiles.\" So if we have tiles from only two suits (and possibly honors), that counts. So if we discard F1, we would have W and T only, that gives 1 point. But we also have F3 pung which is honor, so that might break it? The pattern says \"A hand with exactly two of the three suits of tiles.\" It doesn't say no honors, so honors are allowed. So we could have One Voided Suit (1 point) if we have tiles from only two suits (W and T) and honors. That seems to be the case: we have W and T and honors (F3). So that's 1 point.\n- Other possible: Edge Wait, Closed Wait, Single Wait, Self Drawn, etc., are situational.\n\nSo total points so far: F3 pung (1) + possibly One Voided Suit (1) = 2. We need at least 6 more.\n\nHalf Flush gives 6, so that would bring total to 8 (including the other points). So Half Flush is a good target. To achieve Half Flush, we must have only honor tiles and tiles of one suit. Currently we have honors (F1, and exposed F3 pung) and two suits: W and T. So we need to eliminate either W or T. Eliminating T would mean disca